<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Publication_28">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#Publication"/>
  <reportsReaction rdf:resource="#reaction_instance_28"/>
  <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Publication_28</rdfs:label>
  <openalexId rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">W4399979533</openalexId>
  <score rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">0.9891521</score>
  <publicationDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2024-04-24</publicationDate>
  <doi rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">10.54254/2755-2721/56/20240627</doi>
  <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">DOI: 10.54254/2755-2721/56/20240627</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Title: A review of hydroformylation to produce aldehyde</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Hydroformylation is additionally utilized in specialty synthetic compounds and is connected with the natural amalgamation of aromas and drugs. The advancement of hydroformylation is one of the significant accomplishments of modern science in the twentieth hundred years. Based on the important role of hydroformylation for the industrial production of aldehydes, some studies have been carried out in this paper. The research method used in this paper is literature review. At the beginning of this paper, the definition and application of hydroformylation are introduced, this paper also gives a brief review of the production of aldehyde, several representative applications of the catalytic hydroformylation process including the catalytic system (about metals and ligands), Cobalt-catalysis heavy olefin which about the catalytic cycle and two specific cases. At the end of this review, the paper gives an outlook on hydroformylation while providing a potential solution, such as using extraction, immobilizing the catalyst on a solid support, and using biphasic homogeneous catalytic systems.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

