  <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">DOI: 10.1080/03602458008067535</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Title: The Water-Gas Shift Reaction</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Abstract The water-gas shift is a reversible, exothermic chemical reaction, usually assisted by a catalyst, and is the' reaction of steam with carbon monoxide to produce carbon dioxide and hydrogen gas</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

